  "body": "## Setup Settings screenshots\n\nThe same active milling setup is shown before and after the sheet-job checklist. These images render the shipping Settings page. The before capture removes only the new sheet-job group; the after capture shows the PR head.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Settings before the sheet-job checklist](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/6364a66fe60717dc6792b7abdbc12b35039f0607/3165/settings-before.png) | ![Settings with the sheet-job checklist](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/6364a66fe60717dc6792b7abdbc12b35039f0607/3165/settings-after.png) |\n\n## What changed\n\n- A new undoable command, `SetSheetJob` (`crates/app/src/commands/sheet_job.rs`). It runs the existing `SetStock` and `SetWcsOrigin` commands. It also writes a new setup field, `SetupDef::sheet_job`. One undo restores the stock, the WCS origin and the record.\n- The checklist values are the sheet length (X), width (Y) and thickness, the Z zero (`top` or `spoilboard`), the XY zero (`front_left` by default, the other corners or `centre`), the through-cut allowance and the clamp clearance. All values are in mm.\n- A new post gate clause, `sheet_job::program_problems` (`crates/app/src/sheet_job.rs`). It refuses the post by name in these cases:\n  - a move goes below the sheet bottom minus the allowance;\n  - a rapid that moves in XY is below the sheet top plus the clamp clearance;\n  - the stock thickness or the WCS Z changed after the checklist ran.\n- The project file saves the record as an additive key (no version step). The loader refuses a value that the command would refuse.\n- A new MCP tool, `set_sheet_job`. `allowance` and `z_zero` are required, so an agent always states them. `{\"clear\": true}` removes the record only. `get_job` shows the job. The live gate classifies the tool as `LimitEdit`.\n- A new UI group, \"Sheet job\", on the Settings page of a milling setup. The allowance row is always shown. A summary line gives the deepest Z. Apply queues one `SetSheetJob`. Apply on the page of an inactive setup is refused by name.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3070-sheet-job.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a new feature (P4, the maintainer asked for it). Hobby router users had to know the stock, height and WCS conventions themselves. Nothing stopped a through cut that went into the machine bed.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/mcp_sheet_job.rs`:\n- `one_set_sheet_job_places_stock_and_zero_and_one_undo_puts_them_back`\n- `a_through_cut_within_the_allowance_posts_from_the_stated_zero_and_past_it_is_refused`: the posted lowest Z is Z-10.5 with Z zero on the top and Z-0.5 with Z zero on the spoilboard. An allowance of 0.2 mm refuses the post.\n- `a_rapid_across_below_the_clamp_plane_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_stock_or_zero_edited_after_the_checklist_holds_the_post`\n- `the_sheet_job_survives_a_save_and_reload`: a save and reload keeps the record, and a corrupt allowance is refused at load.\n- `bad_answers_are_refused_with_the_commands_words`\n\nPins in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_settings_page.rs`:\n- `the_sheet_job_checklist_applies_one_undoable_step`\n- `the_sheet_job_checklist_refuses_an_inactive_setup`\n\nAll pins fail on unchanged code, because the tool and the group do not exist there.\n\nMutation checks (each guard turned off, then restored):\n- No gate line in `posting.rs`: the allowance, clamp and drift tests go red.\n- Floor check off: the allowance test goes red.\n- Clamp check off: the clamp test goes red.\n- Z-zero drift check off: the drift test goes red.\n- Loader check off: the save/reload test goes red.\n- `invert` does not undo the steps: the undo test goes red.\n\nEach restore made the suite green again (6/6, then UI 10/10).\n\nGate on the final head:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 472 steps, 0 failed (22.2 min). The schema change reaches every app and ui suite.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe first gate run had one expected red step, `mcp_doc_drift`, because a new tool must be in the docs. The second commit adds `set_sheet_job` to `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md`. It also writes `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` again with the generator command.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. A setup without a sheet job posts the same as before.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A 5-axis or tilted-tool path on a sheet-job setup. The floor check reads the tool-tip Z of each move only.\n- A WCS that is flipped or rotated after the checklist. The checklist sets an identity rotation, and the existing gates judge a later rotation.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese files are shared with open PRs, but this PR changes different functions. Each hunk here is an appended line in a list or a match arm. Whichever PR merges second refreshes.\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (#2714, #2836, #2951 and others): one new line in `verification_report_by`.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `mcp/mod.rs`, `mcp/job.rs` (#2716, #2773, #2920, #3033, #3058, #3061, #3103, #3108, #3158): one registration line each.\n- `crates/app/src/project/apply.rs`, `project/wire.rs` (#2716, #2920): one new field.\n- `crates/app/src/schema.rs`, `commands/mod.rs`, `lib.rs` (#2924, #3061, #3057, #3058): module or field lines.\n\nThe camcraft-mcp skill row for `set_sheet_job` is not in this PR, so the PR changes no process file.\n\nChangelog: Guided sheet job on a milling setup (Settings page and MCP `set_sheet_job`). It sets the sheet stock, Z zero at the sheet top or the spoilboard, XY zero and a stated through-cut allowance as one undo step. The post refuses a cut past the allowance or a rapid below the clamp clearance.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3070\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
